+# release: the first whitespace-delimited field of TSUKUROI_KERNEL_OSRELEASE (default
+# /proc/sys/kernel/osrelease), printed as read; absent -> UNKNOWN (detail osrelease:absent); an
+# entry that is not a readable regular file -> UNKNOWN, unreadable+1 (osrelease:unreadable); an
+# empty first field -> UNKNOWN (osrelease:unparsable).
+# modules_tree: TSUKUROI_KERNEL_MODULES (empty/unset derives /usr/lib/modules/<release> from the
+# release reading; with release UNKNOWN and no override the tree cannot be derived and reads
+# UNKNOWN, detail modules:release-unknown). PRESENT when an existing, readable, searchable
+# directory; ABSENT when no entry exists (modules:absent); otherwise UNKNOWN, unreadable+1
+# (modules:unreadable / modules:not-directory).
+# pkg/pkgver: the owning package of the tree, asked once as `pacman -Qo <dir>` through the shared
+# capture wrapper — and only when the tree is PRESENT. The FIRST line carrying ` is owned by ` in
+# pacman's own order is reported as `<name> <version>`; the answer is never guessed: a failing
+# command (qo:failed), no owner line (qo:unowned), or a tail that is not exactly `<name>
+# <version>` (qo:shape) reads pkg=UNKNOWN pkgver=UNKNOWN; further owner lines are flagged
+# (qo:multi-owner) — pacman -Qo on a modules tree answers with every owning package, the kernel
+# package printed first on the measured host.
+# tainted: the first whitespace-delimited field of TSUKUROI_KERNEL_TAINTED (default
+# /proc/sys/kernel/tainted); absent -> UNKNOWN (tainted:absent); an entry that is not a readable
+# regular file -> UNKNOWN, unreadable+1 (tainted:unreadable); a non-integer -> UNKNOWN
+# (tainted:unparsable). taint_bits decodes only bits 0-19 through the closed bit->log table pinned
+# by S288 (0 P, 1 F, 2 S, 3 R, 4 M, 5 B, 6 U, 7 D, 8 A, 9 W, 10 C, 11 I, 12 O, 13 E, 14 L, 15 K,
